WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:03.267
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.801
I love that you're here.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.334
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:08.434
Do you remember the first time
we met?

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.133
-I do. I remember.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:13.467
This is totally impromptu.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.534
-Yes.
-We were in Minetta Tavern.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.000
-That's correct.
-And you were sitting with

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.634
your parents at a nearby table.
-Yeah.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.067
I was with my mom and my dad.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.067
And my mom goes, "Oh, my God,
that's Clive Davis."

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.234
"Play it cool, Mom.
We're in New York City.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:28.767
We're at Minetta Tavern,
a great restaurant."

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.968
I go, "I got to go over and say
hi to him. It's Clive Davis."

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.968
And so I walked over to you,

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.501
and you were with a group of
people at your table.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.667
It was loud
and the music was on.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:42.868
People were talking, and I go,
"Clive, nice to meet you.

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.067
I'm Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:47.100
And you go...

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.968
And so, I thought you wanted me
to kiss you on the cheek

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.601
because --
-[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.934
I thought this was like
"The Godfather," kiss the ring.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.167
So, I go...

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.467
So I leaned in and I kissed you
on the cheek.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.300
[ Laughter ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.567
And you go -- You go,
"I'm sorry, who are you?"

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:07.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.901
And I go, "I'm so sorry."

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.167
And then I sat back at my table

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.634
and we just made eye contact
the whole night

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.534
'cause I was facing you.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.000
So thank you for putting up
with me and coming back.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.300
I appreciate you being here.
I love you.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.501
And I'm so happy I got to kiss
you on the cheek and I'm sorry.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:26.901
Legend.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.267
Can we talk about this,
by the way?

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:31.033
You just got honored by the
National Portrait Gallery.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.033
Look at this.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.000
David Hockney.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.501
-David Hockney did the portrait,
yes.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.767
One of the bigger thrills
of my life.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.000
-I mean, I love David Hockney.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.534
How did you end up working with
David Hockney?

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:49.834
-Well, when I got word that I
was going to be inducted,

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:54.334
which is a thrill unto itself in
the National Portrait Gallery --

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:56.367
I know David for years.

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.634
He's a friend.
I've been to his studio.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:01.067
He comes to my Grammy party
that I throw

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.267
the night before the Grammys
every year.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.100
-Biggest party of the year.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.868
-And I just called him, and I
said, "David, I'm getting

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.434
one of the biggest lifetime
achievements

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.901
I could possibly get.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:15.200
I'm going to be inducted into
the National Portrait Gallery.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.601
Would you do my portrait?"

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.834
I figured, you know, I got to
take that shot.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.501
-Wow.
-And he said, "You know

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.033
I don't do portraits
from photos.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.667
And I'm in Normandy, France."

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.367
So I said, "I'll be there."

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:32.100
He said, "You'll come for three,
four days."

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.567
I said, "David, I'll come
for three or four days."

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.367
And I did, and he painted it.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.133
-He's the greatest.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.334
[ Applause ]

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:44.200
And now you're in the gallery
forever.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.534
-Now I'm in the gallery.
It was such a thrill.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:49.000
The induction took place
a week ago,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.801
with Serena and Venus Williams
and Ava DuVernay and Dr. Fauci.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.400
it was a wonderful,
wonderful honor.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.501
-You've done so many cool things
in your life.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.634
They call you the man
with the golden ear.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.334
You worked with Springsteen,
Aretha Franklin,

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:09.734
obviously Whitney Houston,
which we're going to get into.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.901
You're an executive producer on
the new film,

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.501
"I Wanna Dance with Somebody."

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:17.467
When you do this, number one,
is it hard to do,

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:21.000
when you think about she's not
with us anymore?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.133
And number two,
why is it important

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.234
that you're involved with this?

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.400
-Well, there had been
a documentary

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.734
and there had been
a television movie.

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.467
Both were wanting.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:36.367
Both did not capture her soul,
her dignity.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.734
They didn't capture everything

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:40.000
everybody wants to know
about her.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.434
And most importantly,
they didn't capture the music.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.901
They didn't capture
those great songs.

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:51.367
They didn't capture that voice
that defined a generation

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:55.167
that was indeed -- She's the
greatest contemporary --

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:59.234
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Absolutely.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:03.934
-And so, this movie does all
that authentically, honestly,

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.167
and the music soars.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.801
-Stanley Tucci plays you.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:11.267
Do you have any notes
for Stanley?

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.133
-You know, I was
very impressed.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:17.067
Before we met, he had read
my autobiography.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.968
He had seen my documentary
on Netflix.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.601
And then we did two Zooms.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:26.767
And I flew up to Boston to meet
him person-to-person.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.567
-Yeah.
-It's a funny experience.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:33.234
But when I saw the film,
I went with him,

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.801
and I felt he is wonderful.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.033
-Yeah. You go, "That's me."

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.267
And do you remember when you
first went into --

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.067
It was here in New York City
where you saw Whitney

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.434
and discovered Whitney.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:46.267
Do you remember where it was
or what she was singing?

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.634
-I remember it vividly.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:53.067
It was at a club called
Sweetwater's on the West Side.

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:56.000
She was background singing for
her mother.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.200
She stepped to the microphone.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.167
She did two songs.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.968
One was "Home" from "The Wiz."

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:08.801
And then, startlingly to me, she
did "The Greatest Love of All."

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:12.901
That, Jimmy, was the song I had
personally commissioned

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.400
eight years earlier
for the movie

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.100
on the life of Muhammad Ali,
"The Greatest."

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.968
And George Benson
had recorded it.

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.868
It was a top 10 R&amp;B record.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:28.934
But coming to the microphone
was this 19-year-old,

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:31.467
stunningly beautiful singer.

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:35.834
And from the beginning of that
song, she was finding

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.801
more meaning in that song

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:41.868
than even the composers,
Michael Masser and Linda Creed,

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.834
could have thought
were in that song.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.467
[ Applause ]

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:48.267
-She just had it.
She just had it in her.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:50.534
I also -- and tell me
if this is true.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.934
If it's not, I'll cut it out of
the show.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.968
But on "I Will Always Love You,"
the beginning,

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:57.400
the a capella part,
was your call.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.834
You said, "Leave this in.
I think you should do that"

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:03.100
and everyone said,
"No, don't start a capella."

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:08.801
-Alright. The facts are that
Kevin Costner suggested it

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.968
to Whitney,
David Foster, and me.

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.534
We all agreed that that would be

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:16.868
a great song
for that airplane scene.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:21.267
And David sent me the -- Right
after Whitney sang it,

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:26.200
he sent me rough mix,
and it did have the a capella,

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.267
and it was raw and was haunting
and so emotionally impactful.

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:34.133
He said, "Look, don't get
demo-itis," they call it.

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:37.434
"I'm working on it. I'm going to
be adding instruments."

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:40.801
So, days passed,
two weeks passed.

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:43.334
Warner Bros. studio
is calling me.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:47.067
We've got to come with a single.
The movie is about to open.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:50.300
I call David.
"Give me your last shot."

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.734
And to me, it came off
a little slick

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:56.133
with the added instrumentation.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:07:00.767
So, when Warners called and I
had to make that decision,

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:04.934
with the a capella intro,
with the raw instrumentation,

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.434
that became the single.

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:10.200
-And so you released that
and it came out.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.567
[ Applause ]

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:15.467
And I don't think anyone was
ready for that.

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:18.434
If it came on your radio,
you're like, "What is this?"

00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:21.267
-Believe me, David was appalled.

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:24.434
But as soon as it came on
the radio, he got more calls

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.901
than he ever received
in his life.

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:31.267
The single is the best-selling
single of all time to this day.

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:32.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:32.534 --> 00:07:34.734
-The secrets behind the song.

00:07:34.734 --> 00:07:36.367
I'm so happy you did that.

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:37.667
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:39.534
Here's a scene from
"I Wanna Dance with Somebody."

00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:40.868
Take a look at this.

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:45.834
-♪ Find your strength in love ♪

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:49.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:55.300
♪♪

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:02.067
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:04.534
-Okay. Just okay.

00:08:04.534 --> 00:08:07.534
I think I might have just heard

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:10.400
the greatest voice of
her generation.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.801
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:13.167
He did a good job.

00:08:13.167 --> 00:08:15.567
That's Clive Davis, everybody.

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:17.534
"I Wanna Dance with Somebody"
is in theaters

00:08:17.534 --> 00:08:19.467
everywhere December 23rd.

